          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હડતાળ — haḍtāḷ — \"a strike (stopping work)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હડતાળથી લોકોને ખૂબ દુઃખ થયું. haḍtāḷthī lokone khūb duḥkh thayũ. The strike caused people a lot of hardship."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હડતાળ (haḍtāḷ) is probably built from haṭ, a market, from Sanskrit haṭṭa, where CDIAL lists the Hindi cousin haṛtāl, the closing of shops in protest (CDIAL 13944), and તાળું, a lock (CDIAL 5749): the market locked up. Work stops: ડ્રાઈવરોની હડતાળ છે, the drivers are on strike."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
